          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most sealed crawl spaces under an average house, the AlorAir Sentinel HD55 is the right buy: it keeps working down to 33.8°F, it is sized correctly for the typical space, and a pump version is available if you have no drain. Choose the Aprilaire E070 for very low crawl spaces, the Santa Fe Compact70 for the tightest access hatches in mild climates, and the HD90 or Advance90 when the space is genuinely large.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you buy, the machine is the last step, not the first. Seal the vents, lay and tape the liner, plan the drain route and put a separate hygrometer at the far end. Do those four things and even a modest unit will hold the crawl space at 50% to 55% for years.
